   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The two grammatical genders",
     "texto": [
      "In Dutch there are two definite articles: «de» (for masculine and feminine words grouped in the common gender, as well as all plurals) and «het» (for neuter words and all diminutives). Since there is no universal fixed rule to predict whether an isolated word takes «de» or «het», the best learning strategy is to memorise each noun from day one together with its article."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
